# The Cartographer, an original A-major orchestral overture by Kimi and SZ.
# Form: woodwind prologue, string theme and answer, cello augmentation, brass development,
# full reprise, and a ritardando coda.
# My structural idea: bars 25-32 give the melody to the cellos in augmentation while the upper
# strings illuminate only alternate bars, leaving silence around their chord windows.
# Chords, one per bar:
# 1-8:   A | E | F#m | D | A/C# | Bm | E | A
# 9-16:  A | E | F#m | D | A/C# | Bm | E | A
# 17-24: D | A/C# | Bm | F#m | D | E | F#m | E
# 25-32: F#m | D | A | E | Bm | F#m | D | E
# 33-40: D | E | C#m | F#m | Bm | E | A | E
# 41-48: F#m | Bm | D | A | Bm | C#m | D | E
# 49-56: A | E | F#m | D | A/C# | Bm | E | A
# 57-64: D | A/C# | Bm | F#m | D | Bm | E | A
title: The Cartographer
composer: Kimi & SZ
about: An original A-major overture. A woodwind draws the first map, the strings take up its bold intervals, and the cellos stretch the melody beneath a half-lit middle section. Brass crosses the rhythmic development before the full orchestra finds its way home.
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
key: A major
style: orchestral
tempo: 96
time: 4/4

@bars 61-64 tempo=96..72

